# Principle 16 — read the composition inventory

Before any schema, compile, adapter, README, host-embed, or “how video
versioning works” work, read [docs/composition.md](docs/composition.md).
Do not wait for the user to name LUT, transitions, codecs, or SFX.

- A video is pads + filters + PTS. Roles are labels, not the IR.
- ffmpeg is the lowerer. Do not invent a compositor.
- Working cache ≠ delivery codec. Bitstream-copy of H.264 slots cannot
  version a post-join look.
- `takes/hook.mov` is not authorship. Hosts bind ranges on library clips.
- Layers `base`/`copy`/`grade`/`legal` are binding opinions, not grade nodes.
- New dimensions are **appended** to `docs/composition.md`. Do not start
  a second inventory. Do not claim the compiler grew because a row exists.
- If a proposed node cannot lower to libavfilter + an encoder, reject it.

```
<!-- BAD -->
swap the hook file, concat -c copy, body stays an 8-bit GOP forever

<!-- GOOD -->
dirty src_hook and every downstream pad; body working-cache may hit;
a LUT after the join still re-filters
```
